{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01382",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.74,
      "end_seconds": 2.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "good afternoon, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.08,
      "end_seconds": 7.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.02,
      "end_seconds": 17.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "Um, so... skipped beats. That's why I came. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.97,
      "end_seconds": 21.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.83,
      "end_seconds": 25.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "It's been about three months, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.59,
      "end_seconds": 33.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.88,
      "end_seconds": 48.43,
      "duration_seconds": 12.55,
      "text": "It's every other day. About a six out of ten. I did try to ignore it for a while. I've been putting this off for weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.31,
      "end_seconds": 53.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.32,
      "end_seconds": 85.28,
      "duration_seconds": 30.96,
      "text": "A flutter in my chest goes along with it, most of the time. Okay, so as for being a bit anxious, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. The flutter in my chest? That's been for about four days. With flutter in my chest, mostly mild"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.74,
      "end_seconds": 103.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Have you had any fainting or dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.85,
      "end_seconds": 110.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Okay, so I haven't had fainting or dizziness, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.37,
      "end_seconds": 116.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Have you had any chest pain or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.06,
      "end_seconds": 123.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "uh, no, I haven't had any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.69,
      "end_seconds": 125.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.72,
      "end_seconds": 128.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.3,
      "end_seconds": 130.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.17,
      "end_seconds": 134.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.28,
      "end_seconds": 137.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.83,
      "end_seconds": 146.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.02,
      "end_seconds": 150.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.13,
      "end_seconds": 156.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.63,
      "end_seconds": 160.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.95,
      "end_seconds": 168.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.25,
      "end_seconds": 173.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.59,
      "end_seconds": 179.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.17,
      "end_seconds": 180.87,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.35,
      "end_seconds": 185.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Herbal calming tea, in the evening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.87,
      "end_seconds": 203.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.26,
      "end_seconds": 206.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Eczema, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.55,
      "end_seconds": 215.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Yes, eczema is known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.35,
      "end_seconds": 228.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.94,
      "end_seconds": 235.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Mm, just a wisdom tooth extraction under sedation, five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.55,
      "end_seconds": 239.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.74,
      "end_seconds": 251.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.51,
      "end_seconds": 281.29,
      "duration_seconds": 11.78,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 99 percent, blood pressure 113 over 79, respiratory rate 18, temperature is 36.8 degrees, pulse is 81 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.42,
      "end_seconds": 287.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "let me look at the area, I'll be gentle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.38,
      "end_seconds": 289.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.77,
      "end_seconds": 309.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Your pulse is regular and your heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.76,
      "end_seconds": 324.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.52,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. So, based on the history and the examination, the most likely explanation is harmless extra heartbeats."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.05,
      "end_seconds": 326.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.93,
      "end_seconds": 338.43,
      "duration_seconds": 10.5,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with harmless extra heartbeats do well once it's treated properly i'd like to arrange an ECG for palpitations"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 339.27,
      "end_seconds": 341.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.47,
      "end_seconds": 365.09,
      "duration_seconds": 21.62,
      "text": "cut back on coffee and energy drinks and keep a diary of when it happens if you faint or have chest pain, that's the point to come in urgently book a review if it carries on after a month is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.29,
      "end_seconds": 370.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "I mean, no, that's all thanks a lot"
    }
  ]
}